.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_PROBE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_probe
.Nd match, probe, and attach a device to a registered driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_probe "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_probe
function matches a device against the drivers registered on its bus, runs the
selected driver's
.Va probe
callback, and binds the device through
.Xr driver_attach 9
if probing succeeds.
.Pp
The function returns
.Dv -EDEFER
when the selected driver indicates that probing must be retried later.
This is a driver-model internal deferral signal and is distinct from ordinary
userspace
.Dv errno
reporting.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn device_probe
function returns 0 on success.
.Pp
It returns:
.Bl -tag -width "-EDEFER"
.It Bq Er ENODEV
The device is
.Dv NULL ,
has no bus, or no registered driver matches it.
.It Bq Er EBUSY
The device is already bound to a driver.
.It Bq Er EDEFER
The selected driver requested deferred probing.
.It Other non-zero values
The selected driver's
.Va probe
or
.Va attach
callback failed and returned an error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus_match_device 9 ,
.Xr driver_attach 9 ,
.Xr driver_register 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn device_probe
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
